      "source": [
        "### M1 Analysis\n",
        "- Did training loss decrease?\n",
        "\n",
        "Yes, steadily, but slowly — it is still declining at epoch 50\n",
        "  (~0.04), so the model has not fully converged yet.\n",
        "\n",
        "- Did validation loss decrease?\n",
        "\n",
        "Yes, and it tracks the training loss closely the whole run.\n",
        "\n",
        "- Is there a large train/validation gap? No — the gap stays under ~0.01 loss / ~1.5 points accuracy for the entire run.\n",
        "\n",
        "- Underfit, overfit, or generalize well?\n",
        "\n",
        "Generalizes well, and if anything is closer to underfitting: with only 1 hidden layer of 32 units it has not hit its capacity limit within 50 epochs."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "e1c0da89",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "e1c0da89"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Task B2 — Medium Network"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 11,
      "id": "70399064",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "70399064"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "def build_medium_model(input_dim: int, output_units: int, output_activation: str) -> keras.Sequential:\n",
        "    model = keras.Sequential([\n",
        "        layers.Input(shape=(input_dim,)),\n",
        "\n",
        "        # TODO: THREE hidden Dense layers\n",
        "        layers.Dense(64, activation=\"relu\"),\n",
        "        layers.Dense(32, activation=\"relu\"),\n",
        "        layers.Dense(16, activation=\"relu\"),\n",
        "\n",
        "        # TODO: Output layer\n",
        "        layers.Dense(output_units, activation=output_activation)\n",
        "    ])\n",
        "    return model"
      ]
    },
